-	<section id="agreement"><h2>Before you use Kredit</h2><p>Read these terms together with the Privacy Notice, the exact sale shown to you before you accepted it, the bank-debit permission and any fee shown to the seller. If you are acting for a business, “you” means that business too.</p><p>By accepting these terms you confirm that you understand them and are allowed to use the account. Accepting these general terms does not force a customer to accept any particular sale. Every single sale needs its own clear yes.</p></section>
-
-	<section id="service"><h2>1. What Kredit does</h2><p class="plain">Kredit writes your sale down and helps you follow the payment. Kredit does not lend you money, does not own the goods, does not choose your customer and cannot promise that anybody will pay you.</p><p>Kredit provides tools that allow an existing seller and customer to:</p><ul><li>record the goods, price, payment day, extra time and any payment plan;</li><li>show the same terms to the customer before the customer says yes;</li><li>keep evidence of acceptance, goods release and customer receipt;</li><li>record payments made to the seller or through an approved provider;</li><li>show the amount still unpaid;</li><li>send account and payment reminders;</li><li>report and review a problem; and</li><li>request an authorised bank debit for an eligible unpaid amount after the agreed time.</li></ul><p><strong>Kredit is not the seller and does not supply the goods.</strong> Kredit does not choose the customer, decide the quality of goods or promise that a customer will pay. In the first release, Kredit does not lend the purchase money to either side. The seller supplies its own goods and allows payment later.</p><p>Kredit is not a bank, wallet, credit bureau, insurance company, marketplace or debt buyer. Any regulated identity, banking or payment function must be performed through an appropriately approved provider. A provider's own terms may also apply to that function.</p></section>
+	<section id="service"><h2>What Kredit does</h2><p>Kredit provides tools that allow an existing seller and customer to:</p><ul><li>record the goods, price, payment day, extra time and any payment plan;</li><li>show the same terms to the customer before the customer says yes;</li><li>keep evidence of acceptance, goods release and customer receipt;</li><li>record payments made to the seller or through an approved provider;</li><li>show the amount still unpaid;</li><li>send account and payment reminders;</li><li>report and review a problem; and</li><li>request an authorised bank debit for an eligible unpaid amount after the agreed time.</li></ul><p><strong>Kredit is not the seller and does not supply the goods.</strong> Kredit does not choose the customer, decide the quality of goods or promise that a customer will pay. The supplier funds the credit sale. The seller supplies its own goods and allows payment later.</p><p>Kredit is not a bank, wallet, credit bureau, insurance company, marketplace or debt buyer. Any regulated identity, banking or payment function must be performed through an appropriately approved provider. A provider's own terms may also apply to that function.</p></section>
 
-	<section id="accounts"><h2>2. Accounts, age and business authority</h2><p class="plain">You must be 18 or older, give correct details and really have the right to act for your business. Keep your codes to yourself. Never share your OTP, backup codes or bank PIN with anybody. Kredit will never ask you for your bank PIN or full card number.</p><ul><li>You must be at least 18 years old and able to enter a binding agreement.</li><li>You must give correct, current information and update it when it changes.</li><li>You must control the phone number or email used for your account.</li><li>If you represent a business, you must have permission to bind or act for it.</li><li>A business does not need a CAC registration number merely to begin setup, but Kredit or a provider may require other proof before money can move.</li><li>You must complete identity, business, bank-account or extra sign-in checks when a sensitive action requires them.</li></ul><p>A business owner may invite staff and choose their roles. The owner is responsible for removing access when a staff member should no longer act. Kredit records important access and account actions.</p><p>Keep your device, sign-in method, OTP, authenticator and recovery codes secure. Do not share them. Tell Kredit quickly if an account or device may have been taken over. Kredit will never ask for your bank PIN or a full card number in a support message.</p></section>
+	<section id="accounts"><h2>Accounts, age and business authority</h2><ul><li>You must be at least 18 years old and able to enter a binding agreement.</li><li>You must give correct, current information and update it when it changes.</li><li>You must control the phone number or email used for your account.</li><li>If you represent a business, you must have permission to bind or act for it.</li><li>A business does not need a CAC registration number merely to begin setup, but Kredit or a provider may require other proof before money can move.</li><li>You must complete identity, business, bank-account or extra sign-in checks when a sensitive action requires them.</li></ul><p>A business owner may invite staff and choose their roles. The owner is responsible for removing access when a staff member should no longer act. Kredit records important access and account actions.</p><p>Keep your device, sign-in method, OTP, authenticator and recovery codes secure. Do not share them. Tell Kredit quickly if an account or device may have been taken over. Kredit will never ask for your bank PIN or a full card number in a support message.</p></section>
 
-	<section id="sale"><h2>3. Making a credit sale</h2><p class="plain">The seller writes the sale. The customer reads it and decides. A sale only becomes real when the customer says yes. After that, nobody can quietly change the goods, the amount or the dates.</p><h3>The seller creates the offer</h3><p>The seller chooses the customer and enters the goods, price, payment date, extra time, payment plan and bank-debit timing. The seller must check these details before sending them. A draft may be changed or deleted before it is sent.</p><h3>The customer checks and accepts</h3><p>The customer receives a private link, confirms the required details and sees the exact sale before accepting. The customer may say no. A sale does not become active merely because the seller created it, sent a link or obtained a general account registration.</p><h3>Accepted terms cannot be secretly changed</h3><p>Kredit keeps a version and protected document hash for accepted terms. A seller cannot replace the accepted amount, goods or dates without a new, lawful agreement. Where the product allows payment dates to be changed, both sides must first agree and the change cannot rewrite a payment already made.</p><h3>Keep your own commercial records</h3><p>Kredit records the transaction in the service but does not replace every invoice, tax record, stock record, warranty or document a business may be required to keep.</p></section>
+	<section id="sale"><h2>Making a credit sale</h2><h3>The seller creates the offer</h3><p>The seller chooses the customer and enters the goods, price, payment date, extra time, payment plan and bank-debit timing. The seller must check these details before sending them. A draft may be changed or deleted before it is sent.</p><h3>The customer checks and accepts</h3><p>The customer receives a private link, confirms the required details and sees the exact sale before accepting. The customer may say no. A sale does not become active merely because the seller created it, sent a link or obtained a general account registration.</p><h3>Accepted terms cannot be secretly changed</h3><p>Kredit keeps a version and protected document hash for accepted terms. A seller cannot replace the accepted amount, goods or dates without a new, lawful agreement. Where the product allows payment dates to be changed, both sides must first agree and the change cannot rewrite a payment already made.</p><h3>Keep your own commercial records</h3><p>Kredit records the transaction in the service but does not replace every invoice, tax record, stock record, warranty or document a business may be required to keep.</p></section>
 
-	<section id="goods"><h2>4. Goods, delivery and problems</h2><p class="plain">The goods are the seller’s responsibility, not Kredit’s. If something is wrong, the customer reports it with proof, and the money in question goes on hold while it is sorted out. The rest of the money may still be due. Do not report a false problem just to delay paying.</p><p>The seller is responsible for the goods, description, price, quality, safety, delivery and any promise made about them. Kredit does not inspect or approve goods.</p><p>After customer acceptance, the seller records when and how the goods leave. The customer confirms receipt or reports a problem. Both sides must act honestly and keep useful evidence such as a delivery number, receipt, photo or document.</p><p>If the customer reports a genuine problem, Kredit may pause bank debit for the amount affected while the matter is reviewed. The remaining undisputed amount may still be due where the accepted sale and applicable law allow it. Reporting a problem does not automatically cancel the full sale, and it must not be used only to delay payment.</p><p>The seller and customer should first try to settle the matter with clear evidence. Kredit may help record the decision or apply a permitted adjustment, but is not a court and may require a formal complaint or external legal process where the issue cannot be resolved in the product.</p></section>
+	<section id="goods"><h2>Goods, delivery and problems</h2><p>The seller is responsible for the goods, description, price, quality, safety, delivery and any promise made about them. Kredit does not inspect or approve goods.</p><p>After customer acceptance, the seller records when and how the goods leave. The customer confirms receipt or reports a problem. Both sides must act honestly and keep useful evidence such as a delivery number, receipt, photo or document.</p><p>If the customer reports a genuine problem, Kredit may pause bank debit for the amount affected while the matter is reviewed. The remaining undisputed amount may still be due where the accepted sale and applicable law allow it. Reporting a problem does not automatically cancel the full sale, and it must not be used only to delay payment.</p><p>The seller and customer should first try to settle the matter with clear evidence. Kredit may help record the decision or apply a permitted adjustment, but is not a court and may require a formal complaint or external legal process where the issue cannot be resolved in the product.</p></section>
 
-	<section id="payments"><h2>5. Payments, balances and Kredit fees</h2><p class="plain">A customer can pay the seller directly or through Kredit. The seller must see the money in their bank before confirming it. If money is reversed later, it becomes owed again. The seller pays Kredit’s fees, not the customer. And only when a sale starts, or when Kredit actually collects money.</p><h3>Payments</h3><p>A customer may pay the seller directly or through an available approved payment method. When a customer reports a direct transfer, the seller must check the seller's bank before confirming it. Kredit reduces the amount left only when the payment is recognised. A reversed or failed payment may make money due again.</p><p>A customer must not pay more than the amount lawfully due. Kredit recalculates the true unpaid amount before any bank-debit request and uses controls intended to prevent duplicate collection. A pending payment, provider delay or reconciliation issue may temporarily stop another money action.</p><h3>Fees paid by the seller</h3><p>Adding a customer or draft sale has no fee. The rates recorded in each offer govern that sale:</p><ul><li>the supplier base service fee applies to activated principal after the required acceptance and goods steps; and</li><li>the recorded additional collection fee applies only to money successfully collected through Kredit at or after the permitted collection time.</li></ul><p>Changing the published rates does not change existing offers. <a href="/pricing">Current pricing</a> applies to new offers. A failed debit does not earn the additional collection fee. A sale cancelled before activation does not earn the base fee. The seller must review the applicable rates before agreeing to the sale.</p><p>The customer pays the accepted price of the goods and any customer charge clearly included in the individual sale and permitted by law. Kredit does not silently add the seller's platform fee to the customer's debt.</p><p>Taxes may apply to Kredit fees. The final invoice and tax treatment will follow applicable law. If a fee or payment record is wrong, use the correction or complaint process; do not edit a completed financial record outside the provided reversal or correction flow.</p></section>
