-	<section id="debit"><h2>6. Bank-debit permission and late payment</h2><p class="plain">Bank debit is a separate permission the customer gives, with a limit on how much can ever be taken. The customer can cancel it at any time. But cancelling it does not cancel money they already owe. A debit can fail, and Kredit cannot promise it will work.</p><p>A customer may be asked to create a separate mandate with a bank or approved payment provider. The mandate is authority for payments within its stated amount, duration and scope. It is not itself proof that the underlying sale is valid, and it does not give Kredit unrestricted access to every account.</p><p>Before a sale is accepted, the customer sees the payment day, extra time and the earliest time an automatic debit may be requested. Kredit may request only an eligible unpaid amount within the accepted terms and active mandate. Reminders, provider availability, a payment claim, a dispute, a risk hold or a legal requirement may change whether or when a request is sent.</p><p>The customer may stop or cancel a mandate through an available provider or Kredit control. Cancelling a mandate stops future use of that permission when the cancellation takes effect; it does not erase money already owed under a valid sale. The customer should arrange another payment method with the seller.</p><p>A bank or provider may reject, delay, partially complete or reverse a request. Kredit does not promise successful collection. Both sides must wait for a final confirmed result before treating an uncertain provider response as payment.</p></section>
+	<section id="debit"><h2>Bank-debit permission and late payment</h2><p>A customer may be asked to create a separate mandate with a bank or approved payment provider. The mandate is authority for payments within its stated amount, duration and scope. It is not itself proof that the underlying sale is valid, and it does not give Kredit unrestricted access to every account.</p><p>Before a sale is accepted, the customer sees the payment day, extra time and the earliest time an automatic debit may be requested. Kredit may request only an eligible unpaid amount within the accepted terms and active mandate. Reminders, provider availability, a payment claim, a dispute, a risk hold or a legal requirement may change whether or when a request is sent.</p><p>The customer may stop or cancel a mandate through an available provider or Kredit control. Cancelling a mandate stops future use of that permission when the cancellation takes effect; it does not erase money already owed under a valid sale. The customer should arrange another payment method with the seller.</p><p>A bank or provider may reject, delay, partially complete or reverse a request. Kredit does not promise successful collection. Both sides must wait for a final confirmed result before treating an uncertain provider response as payment.</p></section>
 
-	<section id="communications"><h2>Messages and electronic records</h2><p class="plain">Kredit will message you about your account, your sales and your payments. You can switch off extra reminders, but not the important messages. What you tap and agree to in the app counts as proof of what happened.</p><p>You agree that Kredit may send required service, security, sale, payment, recovery and complaint messages by the contact method connected to your account. You may control optional messages and quiet hours, but you cannot turn off a message needed to protect the account or complete a transaction.</p><p>Electronic acceptance, timestamps, audit records, provider confirmations and protected document hashes may be used as evidence of what happened. Download or print any record you need for your business. Delivery of a message can fail, so you should also check the account for an important update.</p></section>
+	<section id="communications"><h2>Messages and electronic records</h2><p>You agree that Kredit may send required service, security, sale, payment, recovery and complaint messages by the contact method connected to your account. You may control optional messages and quiet hours, but you cannot turn off a message needed to protect the account or complete a transaction.</p><p>Electronic acceptance, timestamps, audit records, provider confirmations and protected document hashes may be used as evidence of what happened. Download or print any record you need for your business. Delivery of a message can fail, so you should also check the account for an important update.</p></section>
 
-	<section id="responsibilities"><h2>7. What every user must and must not do</h2><p class="plain">Be honest. Do not invent a customer, a delivery, a payment or a problem. Do not use another person’s details. Do not threaten or shame anybody over money. Do not use Kredit for anything against the law.</p><p>You must use Kredit honestly, follow applicable law and cooperate with a reasonable check or correction. You must not:</p><ul><li>create a false person, business, sale, delivery, payment, receipt or dispute;</li><li>use another person's contact, bank or identity information without authority;</li><li>sell illegal, unsafe, stolen or prohibited goods through a Kredit record;</li><li>split, repeat or manipulate a sale to avoid a limit or review;</li><li>attempt to collect money already paid, reversed, adjusted or genuinely disputed;</li><li>harass, threaten, shame or mislead a seller or customer;</li><li>probe, copy, damage or interfere with Kredit or another user's account;</li><li>upload malware or a document you have no right to use; or</li><li>use Kredit to hide fraud, money laundering or another unlawful activity.</li></ul><p>Kredit may limit a document type, transaction size, customer group, business industry, provider, retry or other pilot feature. A displayed limit does not mean Kredit has approved a customer's creditworthiness or guaranteed a transaction.</p></section>
+	<section id="responsibilities"><h2>What every user must and must not do</h2><p>You must use Kredit honestly, follow applicable law and cooperate with a reasonable check or correction. You must not:</p><ul><li>create a false person, business, sale, delivery, payment, receipt or dispute;</li><li>use another person's contact, bank or identity information without authority;</li><li>sell illegal, unsafe, stolen or prohibited goods through a Kredit record;</li><li>split, repeat or manipulate a sale to avoid a limit or review;</li><li>attempt to collect money already paid, reversed, adjusted or genuinely disputed;</li><li>harass, threaten, shame or mislead a seller or customer;</li><li>probe, copy, damage or interfere with Kredit or another user's account;</li><li>upload malware or a document you have no right to use; or</li><li>use Kredit to hide fraud, money laundering or another unlawful activity.</li></ul><p>Kredit may limit a document type, transaction size, customer group, business industry, provider, retry or other service feature. A displayed limit does not mean Kredit has approved a customer's creditworthiness or guaranteed a transaction.</p></section>
 
-	<section id="availability"><h2>When the service is slow or down</h2><p class="plain">We work hard to keep Kredit up and your records correct, but networks, banks and payment companies can fail. If your phone is offline, nothing to do with money is saved. We will never quietly rewrite a sale you already agreed to.</p><p>Kredit aims to keep the service available and records accurate, but maintenance, poor networks, banks, providers or events outside reasonable control may delay a page, message or payment result. Financial actions that require the server are not completed or queued merely because a device is offline.</p><p>We may improve, replace or stop a non-essential feature after reasonable notice. We will not intentionally rewrite an accepted agreement or completed financial history because a feature changes. If a provider becomes unavailable or a result is unknown, Kredit may pause the affected action and reconcile it before trying again.</p></section>
