-	<section id="ending"><h2>8. Suspension, closure and records after closure</h2><p class="plain">You can stop using Kredit, but closing your account does not wipe out money you owe. We may pause an account to protect people, follow the law, or look into something suspicious. Where we can, we will tell you why and how to appeal.</p><p>You may stop using Kredit and ask to close the account, subject to any open sale, payment, dispute, investigation or legal record. Closing an account does not cancel a valid agreement or amount already due.</p><p>Kredit may restrict or suspend an account, business or money action to protect users, obey the law, investigate suspected abuse, respond to a provider issue or enforce these terms. Where safe and lawful, we will explain the reason and how to ask for review. Urgent security action may happen before notice.</p><p>After closure, some information may be kept for the approved legal, financial, fraud-prevention and dispute period. Other information is removed or anonymised under the Privacy Notice.</p></section>
+	<section id="ending"><h2>Suspension, closure and records after closure</h2><p>You may stop using Kredit and ask to close the account, subject to any open sale, payment, dispute, investigation or legal record. Closing an account does not cancel a valid agreement or amount already due.</p><p>Kredit may restrict or suspend an account, business or money action to protect users, obey the law, investigate suspected abuse, respond to a provider issue or enforce these terms. Where safe and lawful, we will explain the reason and how to ask for review. Urgent security action may happen before notice.</p><p>After closure, some information may be kept for the approved legal, financial, fraud-prevention and dispute period. Other information is removed or anonymised under the Privacy Notice.</p></section>
 
-	<section id="legal"><h2>9. Who is responsible for what</h2><p class="plain">The seller answers for the goods. The customer answers for the money they agreed to pay. Kredit answers for running its service properly. Nigerian law applies, and nothing here removes a right Nigerian law says you must have.</p><p>Each seller remains responsible for its goods and each customer remains responsible for a valid accepted payment duty. Kredit remains responsible for providing its service with reasonable care and for rights that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p><p>To the extent allowed by law, Kredit is not responsible for a seller's goods, a customer's business decision, loss caused by false information from a user, or a bank/provider failure outside Kredit's reasonable control. Nothing in these terms removes a right, remedy or responsibility that Nigerian law says cannot be removed. Any limitation in the final approved terms must be fair, clear and proportionate to the service.</p><p>These terms and the Kredit service are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria. The parties should first use the complaint process. If the matter is not resolved, a person may use a competent court or regulator.{data.legal.active ? ` Legal notices may be sent to ${data.legal.entityName}, ${data.legal.serviceAddress}.` : ' The final company and legal-service details will be inserted before these terms become active.'}</p></section>
+	<section id="legal"><h2>Who is responsible for what</h2><p>Each seller remains responsible for its goods and each customer remains responsible for a valid accepted payment duty. Kredit remains responsible for providing its service with reasonable care and for rights that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p><p>To the extent allowed by law, Kredit is not responsible for a seller's goods, a customer's business decision, loss caused by false information from a user, or a bank/provider failure outside Kredit's reasonable control. Nothing in these terms removes a right, remedy or responsibility that Nigerian law says cannot be removed. Any limitation remains subject to mandatory rights under applicable law.</p><p>These terms and the Kredit service are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria. The parties should first use the complaint process. If the matter is not resolved, a person may use a competent court or regulator.{` Legal notices may be sent to ${data.legal.entityName} (RC 9834452), ${data.legal.serviceAddress}.`}</p></section>
 
-	<section id="changes"><h2>If we change these terms</h2><p class="plain">If we change something important, we will tell you first and ask you to agree again where that is needed. The version you agreed to for a particular sale stays with that sale.</p><p>A new version will show its date and important changes. A material change that affects existing users will be communicated before it applies, and a new acceptance will be requested where required. The version accepted for an individual sale remains part of that sale's record. We will not use a later general update to secretly change accepted goods, price or payment dates.</p><p>If one part of these terms cannot be enforced, the remaining parts continue where the law allows. Delay in enforcing a term is not a permanent waiver. You may not transfer an account or agreement without the permissions required by the product and law. Kredit may transfer the service to a lawful successor with appropriate notice and protection of user rights.</p></section>
