-	<section id="help"><h2>10. Help, complaints and regulators</h2><p class="plain">Tell us first, through Help and complaints. Give us the Kredit number, the date, the amount and what you expected. Never send your password, OTP, bank PIN or card number. If we do not sort it out, you can go to a Nigerian regulator or a court.</p><p>Use <a href="/legal/complaints">Help and complaints</a> and include the Kredit reference, date, amount, what happened and the result you expect. Never send your password, OTP, bank PIN or full card number.</p>{#if data.legal.active}<p>You may also email <a href={`mailto:${data.legal.legalEmail}`}>{data.legal.legalEmail}</a> or write to {data.legal.entityName}, {data.legal.serviceAddress}.</p>{/if}<p>If the concern is not resolved, you may use a competent Nigerian regulator or court. Consumer concerns may fall within the remit of the <a href="https://fccpc.gov.ng/" rel="noreferrer">Federal Competition and Consumer Protection Commission</a>. Privacy complaints may be made to the <a href="https://www.ndpc.gov.ng/" rel="noreferrer">Nigeria Data Protection Commission</a>. A bank or payment-provider complaint may also need the provider's process or the appropriate financial regulator.</p></section>
